  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multi-profile with avgpool (config_002, acc=0.591) is the clear best so far, substantially outperforming single-profile (0.485), transformer aggregation (0.519), and image-only (0.208). This establishes multi-profile + avgpool as the optimal profile/aggregation setting for RNA. Uncertainty: whether a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) can capture non-linear structure beyond PCA and push accuracy higher in this best setting. This experiment (config_005: RNA, multi-profile, scvi_n200, avgpool) directly isolates the encoder effect by changing only the RNA encoder from PCA to scvi while holding profile and aggregation at their best-known values, enabling a clean 1:1 comparison with config_002. This is the best use of the 5th experiment because it exploits the strongest direction found, tests the most impactful remaining design choice (representation), and with 5 slots left, establishing the best RNA-only baseline before attempting multimodal fusion is the logical priority given how weak the image signal is (0.208)."
